# Environment variables used by the workflows and the API

Set these in `.env` (copied from `.env.example`). Docker Compose forwards them to both services.
The n8n container must have `N8N_BLOCK_ENV_ACCESS_IN_NODE=false` (already set in `docker-compose.yml`)
so workflow expressions can read `$env`. If you run n8n without Docker, set it in the shell first.

## Safe defaults (do not change without understanding the consequence)

    JOB_MATCH_THRESHOLD=75
    MANUAL_APPROVAL_REQUIRED=true
    AUTOMATIC_SUBMISSION_ENABLED=false
    AI_ENABLED=false
    PLAYWRIGHT_HEADLESS=false

The API refuses to start and the master workflow stops if `MANUAL_APPROVAL_REQUIRED` is not `true`
or `AUTOMATIC_SUBMISSION_ENABLED` is not `false`.

## Full list

    JOB_AUTOMATION_API_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8000     # from Docker n8n to a Windows-hosted API: http://host.docker.internal:8000
    JOB_MATCH_THRESHOLD=75                           # percent, 0-100
    MAX_JOBS_PER_RUN=50
    MAX_APPLICATIONS_PER_DAY=10
    MANUAL_APPROVAL_REQUIRED=true
    AUTOMATIC_SUBMISSION_ENABLED=false
    AI_ENABLED=false
    AI_PROVIDER=none                                 # none | mock | openai_compatible
    AI_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:11434/v1            # openai_compatible only; a non-local host needs https and AI_ALLOW_REMOTE=true
    AI_MODEL=                                        # required for openai_compatible
    AI_API_KEY=                                      # only if the endpoint needs one; .env only, never a workflow
    AI_TIMEOUT=60                                    # seconds
    AI_MAX_INPUT_CHARS=8000
    AI_ALLOW_REMOTE=false
    DATABASE_PATH=data/job_tracker.db
    SCREENSHOT_DIRECTORY=screenshots
    RESUME_DIRECTORY=resumes
    APPROVAL_TOKEN_EXPIRY=3600                       # seconds
    PLAYWRIGHT_HEADLESS=false
    PLAYWRIGHT_SLOW_MO=250                           # milliseconds
    PLAYWRIGHT_TIMEOUT=30000                         # milliseconds
